  "instructions": [
    "In a medium bowl, whisk together miso paste, lemon juice, 1 tablespoon olive oil, garlic, cumin, smoked paprika, and black pepper.",
    "Add the chicken breast to the bowl and marinate for at least 30 minutes, or up to 2 hours in the refrigerator.",
    "Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large Dutch oven or clay tagine over medium-high heat.",
    "Remove the chicken from the marinade, letting any excess liquid drip off.",
    "Add the chicken to the pot and sear until browned on all sides, about 5-7 minutes.",
    "Add the onion salt, diced tomatoes, and chicken broth to the pot.",
    "Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer, covered, until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened, about 25-30 minutes.",
    "Season the tagine with salt and pepper to taste.",
    "Garnish with chopped parsley, if desired.",
    "Serve hot over couscous or rice, if desired."
  ],
